---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../components/landing/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../components/landing/Footer.astro';

const title = "SECURITY";
---

<Layout>
  <div class="fixed inset-0 noise-bg pointer-events-none z-50"></div>
  <div class="fixed top-[-10%] right-[-5%] w-[600px] h-[600px] gradient-sphere pointer-events-none -z-10"></div>
  
  <Navbar />
  <main class="relative pt-32 max-w-[1600px] mx-auto px-8 min-h-screen">

<!-- Hero Section -->
<section class="relative grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-12 items-start mb-24">
    <div class="lg:col-span-8">
        <h1 class="font-headline text-7xl md:text-9xl font-bold tracking-tighter leading-tight mb-8">
            SECURITY<br/>
            <span class="gradient-text">POSTURE</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="font-body text-on-surface-variant text-xl max-w-xl leading-relaxed">
            TajsOS is designed with a fundamental principle: your data belongs on your device first. We are building towards a robust local-first architecture.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- Details Section -->
<section class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-8 mb-32">
    <div class="glass-panel p-8 rounded-xl">
        <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary text-4xl mb-6">database</span>
        <h3 class="font-headline text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Local First</h3>
        <p class="text-on-surface-variant font-body leading-relaxed">
            By default, all data is stored in a local SQLite database on your device. There are no mandatory cloud dependencies or centralized SaaS servers that hold your primary data. Your data, your device.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="glass-panel p-8 rounded-xl">
        <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary text-4xl mb-6">sync_alt</span>
        <h3 class="font-headline text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Experimental Sync</h3>
        <p class="text-on-surface-variant font-body leading-relaxed">
            The project includes an experimental synchronization server for cross-device usage. This server is meant to be self-hosted. It currently relies on bearer token authentication, but full end-to-end encryption (E2EE) is a planned future feature, not yet implemented.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="glass-panel p-8 rounded-xl">
        <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary text-4xl mb-6">code</span>
        <h3 class="font-headline text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Open Source Status</h3>
        <p class="text-on-surface-variant font-body leading-relaxed">
            The codebase is open and experimental. We do not offer commercial security guarantees, enterprise SLAs, or external security audits at this time. Use the software understanding that it is under active development.
        </p>
    </div>

    <div class="glass-panel p-8 rounded-xl">
        <span class="material-symbols-outlined text-primary text-4xl mb-6">shield</span>
        <h3 class="font-headline text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Vulnerability Reporting</h3>
        <p class="text-on-surface-variant font-body leading-relaxed">
            If you find a security issue in the local implementation or the experimental sync server, please open an issue or contact the maintainers via the repository.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
